    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field so it returns `true` when an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the 50 limit), leaving the hard 409 rejection at 50 untouched.\n\nChanges, kept as small cohesive units to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n2. **New `CityCapacity.java`** \u2014 a tiny stateless helper (single static method, no surrounding class complexity) mirroring the existing `BulkSignup` pattern. It counts owners with an exactly-matching city and returns `count >= 40 && count < RequireCityCapacity.CAPACITY`, reusing the existing `CAPACITY = 50` constant so the two thresholds can't drift apart.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) and **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 one added line each, `dto.setCapacityWarning(CityCapacity.approaching(owner.getCity(), ownerRepository))`, alongside the existing derived-field assignments.\n\nEach touched function stays trivially simple (one new line, WMC_other \u2248 0 in these tiny classes), and the counting logic lives in its own small unit rather than growing any existing method or the hard-limit class.\n\nThe acceptance suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0).",
